    "result_text": "The build is green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event for owner creation. The change satisfies the spec: alongside the existing human-readable audit line, each create now emits an immutable JSON event via the `AUDIT` logger.\n\n**What I added:**\n\n1. **`OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** (new) \u2014 an immutable Java `record` capturing `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event}`. Being a record, it can never be mutated after construction. A convenience constructor stamps `event` to the `OWNER_CREATED` discriminator constant.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 wired it into the create flow:\n   - A shared thread-safe `ObjectMapper` (Jackson 3, `tools.jackson.databind`) serializes the event to JSON.\n   - A static `AtomicLong CREATE_SEQUENCE` supplies `seq` \u2014 a strictly increasing, per-JVM value assigned atomically so concurrent creates get distinct, monotonic numbers.\n   - `emitOwnerCreatedEvent(owner)` is called right after the existing audit line in `createOwner`, logging e.g. `{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`.\n\n**The forward-compatibility requirement:** the event's identifier value flows through a single `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` method that returns `owner.getCustomerCode()` today. The spec's key requirement \u2014 \"whatever replaces it later (so when the customerCode is unified into the memberId, the event carries the memberId instead)\" \u2014 is met by that one indirection point: when the identifier is unified into a `memberId`, only `primaryIdentifier` changes and the event automatically carries the new primary identifier, with no other change to the create flow.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier`) passes \u2014 it confirms an `AUDIT` line contains `OWNER_CREATED`, the owner id, and the owner's `customerCode`. **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.**",
